  "description": "YAVYUS crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C79 H138 N2 O42 P6 Tb5,4(C1 H4 O1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Tb2 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb5 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 3 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.870-3.930 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 105.09-108.67°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Tb5(μ3-OH)(NO3)2(dipp)6(CH3OH)7(H2O)4]·4CH3OH·H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
